CE-6-67-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":67,"verse":32,"english":"And stationed in his chariot that mighty carwarrior disturbed all quarters with his arrows and pierced Dasaratha's sons with sharp shafts won by him.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.689,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-80-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6067032","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aec9ef0ad9e6d39051fc1687d1ce553b839dde0798bcb8c0fdb05d263d054d2d","compact":"fa29ea9763ce9ee90c6c71834f7a1f8ca4f1995d60cf640c080801db32a60983","nasal":"fa29ea9763ce9ee90c6c71834f7a1f8ca4f1995d60cf640c080801db32a60983"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-67-33","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":67,"verse":33,"english":"Being greatly hurt with those sharp-pointed and terrible arrows Rāma and Lakşmaņa appeared like blossoming kingsukas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-80-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6067033","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c5ac9a6def8ea6af34297b4f89c49061eed393bcdd804819af50f78115fd381","compact":"2054b347fdcbc62b038f602b88529d88e2806bb5fd5caa02579594674ebb31dd","nasal":"fad50f0930e16052e4d5d72828a5b4035e6ce05fa1d70c2325be2d0962c2e87c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-67-34","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":67,"verse":34,"english":"Like to the sun hidden in clouds they could see neither his countenance and motion, nor his bow and arrows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.681,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-80-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6067034","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b2ec49b46e05fbb7f9bb8f65ee6497fd304fb00df2d0cc7cbce8ea368b4a31dc","compact":"567a342af209b67a6663c1158b46128411c9029b34a624327d14783e8117420